{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01BvaXKPCezx52DLFaBdnxZq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both gates green with the revised CLI contract: `view pull` now emits the message array itself on stdout, `view materialize` prints the written path, failures stay structured OpResult errors with exit 1, and the status/compact/sweep parity legs are unchanged.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Resolved verifier finding S5-001 only. In src/cli/view.ts, `view pull` now prints the message array itself as JSON on stdout on success (the AC-5.5/TC-5.4 contract: the array IS the product, not an OpResult envelope), and `view materialize` prints the written path itself on stdout. Both commands fall through to the existing renderResult on failure, so every failure case still exits nonzero with the structured OpResult error JSON (missing-thread and unknown-format legs unchanged and still passing). status, compact, and sweep are untouched and keep printing the SDK result JSON, preserving their parity coverage. The --help blurb names the two success-output exceptions. cli-process-view.test.ts now asserts the story contract directly: the pull parity leg and the CLI-advance leg parse stdout as a ViewMessage[] and compare it to the SDK pull's messages; the materialize leg asserts stdout.trim() equals the --out path before validating the file. Manifest hash re-recorded for the modified process test; both gates rerun green.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/cli/view.ts\", \"reason\": \"S5-001: pull success prints the message array JSON, materialize success prints the written path; failures keep the structured OpResult error JSON with exit 1; header comment documents the contract\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"help text names the two success-output exceptions (pull → array, materialize → path) so the printed contract matches behavior\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-view.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"pull/materialize spawned legs assert the story contract directly (parse stdout as the array / compare stdout to the path) instead of unwrapping OpResult; status/compact/sweep parity legs untouched\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"re-recorded hash for the amended cli-process-view.test.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"cli-process-view: 'spawned pull emits the message array itself as JSON; spawned status matches; both equal the SDK's reads of the same thread' (parses stdout as ViewMessage[], compares to SDK pull messages)\",\n      \"cli-process-view: 'spawned materialize prints the written path; the file parses, conforms, and is byte-identical to the SDK's' (asserts stdout.trim() === --out path)\",\n      \"cli-process-view: CLI-intake-advances-boundary leg (pull stdout parsed as the message array)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 325,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 0\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"S5-001: view pull and view materialize success output now match the story contract (top-level message array / bare written path) at the spawned-process boundary, asserted directly without OpResult unwrapping\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Pull emits the array on success with or without --json (the flag remains a grammar-compatible no-op since JSON is the only output shape); the pull's ViewMeta no longer crosses the CLI on success — operators read those numbers via view status, and failures still carry the full structured error\",\n      \"Failure-case output is deliberately asymmetric with success output for these two commands (structured OpResult J